{"kind":"article","sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Deliver events to your logs, your traces, a server or memory, and decide what each destination may see."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack"],"title":"Essentials"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChoosingDestinations","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Destination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a plain sink: ","type":"text"},{"code":"deliver(to:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" hands it each batch of records. Traffluent ships a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"few, each in a module of its own, so an app links only the ones it uses.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Logs-and-traces","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Logs and traces"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To see events beside your logs or traces, deliver to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LoggerDestination(logger:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoggingDestinations\/documentation\/LoggingDestinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":") or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SpanEventDestination(tracer:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":")."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Only apps that use swift-log or swift-distributed-tracing this way link them. A span event joins"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the span that was active when the event was tracked, even if delivery runs later."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"A-server","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"A server"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To send batches to a server, deliver to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination(endpoint:headerFields:encoder:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). It posts each batch as one request whose body is what your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"writes for it, so events need no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance and the wire format is yours. A failed send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is logged and dropped, without holding up the other destinations. It sends with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":" by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default, or through any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPTransport"},{"type":"text","text":" you pass as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transport:"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The bootstrapped tracing instrument, or the one you pass as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"instrument:"},{"type":"text","text":", injects the trace"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context of the batch’s first record into the request’s header fields, so a server that extracts it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"joins the request to the app’s trace. The encoder’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Content-Type"},{"type":"text","text":" always wins, and with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instrument bootstrapped no header is added. Only the first record’s context travels in the header"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fields; write each record’s context into the body if the server needs it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To send to a self-hosted TraffluentCollector, give ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorBatchEncoder(plan:)"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding","isActive":true},{"text":") as its encoder, and the collector’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"API key as an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Authorization: Bearer"},{"text":" header field. It writes the collector’s ingest format: each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record’s identifier (which a redelivered record keeps), its name, timestamp and redelivery marker,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its properties read through the event’s schema in your ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"text":", and its standard context and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trace context. A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"text":" value is sent only while the record reveals it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Memory","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Memory"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To read what was tracked inside the app, deliver to an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"InMemoryDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" as well (module"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"): for an event inspector in a debug build, a recent-activity view, a SwiftUI"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"preview, or a test of what your code tracks. It keeps the newest 1,000 records, or as many as you"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pass as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capacity:"},{"type":"text","text":", dropping the oldest across batches; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"InMemoryDestination.unbounded()"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every one. Read it with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events(of: SignedUp.self)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"records"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batches"},{"type":"text","text":", or wait on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deliveries"},{"type":"text","text":", which announces each batch to one reader."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Sensitive-values-and-call-sites","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Sensitive values and call sites"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A property that destinations shouldn’t see unless they must is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value. A destination","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reads it only through the record, with ","type":"text"},{"code":"reveal(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and printing or mirroring it shows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"<redacted>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"code":"redactingSensitiveValues()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" makes a destination’s records reveal nothing, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"droppingCallSite()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" removes their call sites. Every other destination receives both:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct SignedIn: Event {","    var email: Sensitive<String>","}","","let backend = InMemoryDestination()","let vendor = InMemoryDestination()","let tracker = Tracker()","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(","    to: backend,","    vendor.redactingSensitiveValues().droppingCallSite()",")","tracker.track(SignedIn(email: Sensitive(\"ada@example.com\")))","await tracker.finish()","try await delivery.execute()","let event = backend.events(of: SignedIn.self)[0]","let email = backend.records[0].reveal(event.email)    \/\/ \"ada@example.com\"","let redacted = vendor.records[0].reveal(event.email)  \/\/ nil","let callSite = vendor.records[0].sourceLocation       \/\/ nil"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accepting(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" narrows a destination to the consent categories it serves ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"role":"article","title":"Choosing Destinations"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"]}],"references":{"doc://Destinations/documentation/Destinations":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","role":"collection","title":"Destinations","url":"\/documentation\/destinations","type":"topic"},"doc://TracingDestinations/documentation/TracingDestinations":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations","role":"collection","title":"TracingDestinations","url":"\/documentation\/tracingdestinations","type":"topic"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","role":"collection","title":"HTTPDestinations","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","type":"topic"},"doc://CollectorEncoding/documentation/CollectorEncoding":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding","role":"collection","title":"CollectorEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/collectorencoding","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","title":"Traffluent","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingEvents":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track typed events with a tracker, then deliver them in batches to any number of destinations."}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingevents","title":"Tracking Events"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TestingWhatYouTrack":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run a test’s body with a fresh tracker and check the events it tracked."}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/testingwhatyoutrack","title":"Testing What Your Code Tracks"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingFromViews":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Give views the tracker the way each framework passes values down, and let modifiers and controls track what views do."}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingfromviews","title":"Tracking from SwiftUI, UIKit and AppKit"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ConsentGating":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Deliver an event only once the user grants the purpose it is collected for."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","role":"article","title":"Consent Gating","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/consentgating","type":"topic"},"doc://LoggingDestinations/documentation/LoggingDestinations":{"abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoggingDestinations\/documentation\/LoggingDestinations","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/loggingdestinations","title":"LoggingDestinations","type":"topic"}}}